Castlora (the website, the web app, the Android app, their code, texts, icons and other content, together "the Software") is free to use, but it is not open source. The source code is not published. The Software is made only to be used: the website and web app to be visited and used, and the Android app (APK) to be downloaded from the official download page and installed.

The official website and web app are at https://william-lindberg.github.io/castlora/ and the official download page for the Android app is https://github.com/William-Lindberg/castlora/releases.

1. What you may do

Free of charge, you may:
a. use the website and the web app, and download the Android app from the official download page and install it on your own devices, for your own personal, non-commercial use;
b. use it within a non-commercial group (for example a family, a chess club, a school or a community) as long as nobody is charged for access to Castlora itself;
c. make backups of your own data, and share content you made yourself (for example your own games and the backup files you export).

